.TH XUR.STD.MATH 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.math \- mathematical functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::math;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::math
provides basic mathematical operations on numbers.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B sqrt(x: f64) -> f64
Square root.
.TP
.B pow(x: f64, y: f64) -> f64
Raise
.I x
to the power
.IR y .
.TP
.B abs(x: f64) -> f64
Absolute value.
.TP
.B min(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
The smaller of two integers.
.TP
.B max(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
The larger of two integers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::math;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    io::println("sqrt(9) = {}", math::sqrt(9.0));
    io::println("2^10 = {}", math::pow(2.0, 10.0));
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.num (7)
